# Applies to every image built with the repo root as context (docker/builder.Dockerfile,
# docker/service.Dockerfile). Every Dockerfile here either doesn't need these paths at all, or
# regenerates them fresh inside the container (`pnpm install`, `tsc`/`next build`) — carrying the
# host's copies in only bloats the build-context upload and risks shadowing the container's own
# linux/glibc-built native modules with host-platform ones at the exact same path.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/generated/prisma
.git
infra/cdk/cdk.out
infra/cdk/node_modules
*.log

# Never ship a host's environment into a build. `docker/web.Dockerfile` copies the whole workspace,
# and `clients/web`'s Vite build now reads the root `.env` — so a developer's file would put its
# `VITE_*` values into the bundle. `VITE_VERIFY_API_URL` is protected by the Dockerfile's own `ENV`
# (process.env wins over a .env file in Vite), but `VITE_ENABLE_AGGREGATOR` has no such guard,
# and that one is TRD §1.4's boundary. The secrets in the same file are reason enough on their own.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
